Say whether the arbitration unlock returns

run-370's panel repeats U1 U2T a dozen times: the global lock is free, it is
taken, and unlockForArbitration is entered again and again.  That is not a
deadlock on the lock -- the console simply stopped printing, and matching keeps
going behind it.

Mark the end of the function: U3 after each return says the whole lock/unlock
path completes, which turns 'how far did matching get' into something the
framebuffer can answer.
---
diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
index 565a0e3..fb25aa6 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
@@ -2035,6 +2035,10 @@ IOService::unlockForArbitration( void )
 
 	// unlock global access
 	IOUnlock( gArbitrationLockQueueLock );
+	/* nio: the function ran to the end.  run-370 showed U1 U2T over and over,
+	 * so the global lock is free and this path repeats; U3 says whether each
+	 * of those calls also returns. */
+	nio_u_mark(" U3");
 }
 
 uint32_t
